# What it does

[TypeSafe](https://docs.typesafe.ai) models such as Jev answer *questions about
state* with calibrated probabilities instead of generated text. There are three
kinds of question:

- **noul**: a yes/no question. The answer is the probability of yes.
- **choice**: pick one option from a set you define.
- **score**: rate against ordered levels you define.

`tai` wraps the [HTTP API](https://docs.typesafe.ai/api) with a typed DSL.
You describe your questions as a Zig struct literal, and `tai` works out the
result type at compile time. Choice options become a real `enum`, so a
`switch` on the answer is checked for exhaustiveness.

```zig
const r = try client.ask("Help! My payouts have been failing for 3 days.", .{
    .is_urgent = tai.noul("Does this convey urgency?"),
    .department = tai.choice("Which team should handle this?", .{
        .billing = "Payments, invoicing, refunds",
        .technical = "Bugs, outages, integrations",
        .sales = "Pricing, upgrades, new accounts",
    }),
    .frustration = tai.score("How frustrated is the customer?", .{ "Calm", "Frustrated", "Very angry" }),
}, .{});

if (r.answers.is_urgent > 0.8) page(oncall);

switch (r.answers.department.choice) {
    .billing => route(billing),
    .technical => route(engineering),
    .sales => route(sales),
}
```

# Install

`tai` targets Zig `0.17.0-dev` and has no dependencies beyond the standard
library.

```sh
zig fetch --save git+https://github.com/benomahony/zig-typesafe-ai
```

Then, in `build.zig`:

```zig
const tai = b.dependency("tai", .{ .target = target, .optimize = optimize });
exe.root_module.addImport("tai", tai.module("tai"));
```

# Quick start

Get an API key from TypeSafe and export it:

```sh
export TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...
```

```zig
const std = @import("std");
const tai = @import("tai");

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !void {
    var client: tai.Client = try .init(init.gpa, init.io, .{
        .environ_map = init.environ_map,
    });
    defer client.deinit();

    const r = try client.ask("I was charged twice. Please help.", .{
        .billing = tai.noul("Is this about billing?"),
    }, .{});

    std.debug.print("billing: {d:.2} ({s})\n", .{ r.answers.billing, r.model() });
}
```

`ask` returns a plain value that owns no heap memory, so there is nothing to
free.

